# Swift Package Registry (T-P5-SWIFT): SwiftPM (swift 6.4) resolves a small public package through an SCM-backed
# proxy of github.com (tags from the ref advertisement, the tag's tarball repackaged into a pinned, deterministic
# source archive), by registry identity and through --replace-scm-with-registry (/identifiers); publishes a package
# to a hosted registry with an API token and resolves it back; the negative auth cases are refused. SwiftPM talks to
# registries over HTTPS only: the client reaches the plain-HTTP harness stack through go/tlsfront.go
# (tests/clients/README.md; Documents/Operations/clients/swift.md).

# The Git host (smart-HTTP ref advertisement, tag archive) and the archive's redirect target.
HOSTS="github.com codeload.github.com"
# swift:6.4.3-noble with curl, zip/unzip and the TLS front (compose.harness.yaml client-swift).
CLIENT=swift
NEEDS_STACK=1
# JohnSundell/Files 4.2.0: its ref advertisement (about 8 KB) and one tag tarball (about 170 KB). Budget 1 MiB.
FIXTURE_BUDGET_KB=1024
FIXTURE_FILE_MAX_KB=512
